course: dictionary
lesson: 14578
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Pixie» can mean a make-believe creature, a cheeky child, or a short hairstyle. To pick the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues.
explain: «The pixie hid the key under a mushroom.» The clues are hid and mushroom, which belong to a story, so a pixie here is a tiny make-believe creature. Always ask: what does the whole sentence tell me? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Our little pixie will not sit still, and she keeps giggling at her brother.» Here pixie means a small, lively, cheeky child. The words not sit still and giggling are the clues. Informal words like this often describe a person, not a creature.
explain: «Mia's new pixie cut is very short at the back.» The clue is cut, which tells you this is a hairstyle. Pixies from stories are not real, but a pixie cut is a real haircut that people have.
fact: A pixie is a small make-believe creature in stories, like a tiny elf or fairy with pointed ears.
fact: Pixies love mischief, so they often play tricks, hide things or grant wishes in old tales of England and Cornwall.
fact: Informally, a pixie can be a small, lively, cheeky child.
fact: A pixie cut is a very short hairstyle, and a pixie hat is a hat with a point.
fact: Pixies are not real: they live in stories and folklore, so a sentence about a pixie hiding a key is make-believe.
exercise: «The pixie hid the key under a mushroom.» What is a pixie in this sentence? | A type of bicycle | A large farm animal | A kind of mushroom | *A small make-believe creature from a story
exercise: «Our little pixie will not sit still and keeps giggling.» What does pixie mean here? | A quiet, sleepy cat | A wise old teacher | A tall, serious adult | *A small, lively, cheeky child
exercise: «Mia's new pixie cut is very short at the back.» What is a pixie cut? | A long plait down the back | *A very short hairstyle | A garden shed with a roof | A pointed hat with a bell
test:
«The pixie in the story granted her three wishes.» Why is this sentence about make-believe? | *Pixies belong to stories and folklore, not to real life | Pixies are real birds that live in gardens | Pixies are a kind of hairstyle | Pixies are always grown-up and serious | ? 
test:
Mum says, «Tom is a real pixie this morning!» He is giggling, tricking his sister and running around. What does pixie mean here? | *A cheeky, lively child | A make-believe creature with wings | A very short haircut | A pointed hat
exam:
«Her pixie cut made her look bright and cheerful.» Which meaning of pixie fits this sentence? | *A very short hairstyle | A small make-believe creature | A cheeky child | A pointed hat with a bell
